      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Jagged B2/FCC interfaces create local stress concentrations that initiate cracks.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At approximately 750°C, the L12 order parameter decreases.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The decrease in L12 ordering at approximately 750°C reduces antiphase-boundary energy and restores cross-slip.",
